WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
You sound like a
pathologically terrible dad.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.990
And now you have a podcast called Dads

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:12.990
and it's on my podcast
network and you're hosting.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.566
And this is a podcast where

00:00:15.566 --> 00:00:18.500
it's not just a podcast for dads.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.120
You're talking about a
lot of different issues

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.200
involving fatherhood, is that correct?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.600
That is correct.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.090
Myself and Ruthie Wyatt, who you know,

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.900
we cohost the show together

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.810
and we have on different
guests like yourself.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.220
Today is the first episode that drops.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.220
And for everyone who listens,
Conan made us have him on.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.330
He said, if you want this thing to work,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.970
you gotta have the hot
stuff right up front.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:45.803
[Conan] Yup.

00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:47.350
So he was our first episode.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.310
And yeah we talk about being a dad.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.520
We talk about having a dad.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.230
It's not just for dads though.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.865
We also have non-dads on
the show that we interview

00:00:55.865 --> 00:00:58.390
to get perspectives about parenting

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.330
and their relationships
with their dads or stepdads.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.650
Yeah, I had a really
good time talking to you.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.240
And like I said, I did
think it was important

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.190
when you launch a podcast,

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.960
you have to have the hot stuff.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:11.960
That's what I said.

00:01:12.952 --> 00:01:15.410
And that is available for everybody

00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:16.700
wherever you get your podcasts.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.520
You can check out our
interview with Conan right now.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.990
And then once a week, we'll
be releasing a new episode.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.330
We have so many coming up, John Leguizamo,

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.660
David Cross, Sabrina
Jalees, Vanessa Ragland,

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.651
the list goes on and on.

00:01:31.651 --> 00:01:35.080
Andrew Richter, one of our guests.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:35.913
We call him Andy.

00:01:35.913 --> 00:01:36.830
We call him Andy.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:37.663
Not me.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:38.850
He makes me call him Andrew.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.353
Sir Andrew Richter.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.173
Sir?

00:01:42.173 --> 00:01:43.580
You have to call him Sir Andrew Richter?

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.413
Wow.

00:01:44.413 --> 00:01:45.342
Yeah, I asked, I was like,

00:01:45.342 --> 00:01:46.820
don't you have to be knighted?

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.810
But he said that is
technically his first name.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.110
Andrew is his middle name.

